# klipper — klippy host (system python3). Supervised by dinit (no
# start-stop-daemon, no pidfile). NO jemalloc: on real hardware jemalloc's
# LD_PRELOAD corrupts klippy's NEON/thumb2 c_helper.so heap and it aborts
# ("free(): invalid size") right after reaching ready — glibc malloc runs it
# cleanly. Klippy keeps its own structured log via -l; the UDS at
# /tmp/klippy_uds matches moonraker.conf.
#
# Real-time scheduling: launched under SCHED_RR (prio 5) via chrt so klippy and
# every thread it spawns (threads inherit the policy) preempt moonraker, the web
# UI and the camera on the dual-core T113. This is what stops CPU-contention
# "Timer too close" / MCU-timeout underruns under load. The low priority plus the
# kernel RT throttle (sched_rt_runtime_us, 95% of a core) keep a runaway from
# hard-locking the system. dinit re-applies it on every (re)start. chrt is the
# busybox applet (CONFIG_CHRT=y). dinit exposes `nice` but no RT-policy setting,
# hence chrt in the command.
type = process
command = /usr/bin/chrt -r 5 /usr/bin/python3 /opt/klipper/klippy/klippy.py /etc/reforge/printer.cfg -a /tmp/klippy_uds -l /var/log/klippy.log
depends-on = prepare
depends-on = eboard
restart = true
